    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Phyllanthusfluitans(028TC)/22848",
      "html": "<p>Originating from the American tropics, Phyllanthus fluitans is a floating plant of the Phyllanthaceae family. It is similar to Salvinia, differing only in the single-leaf structure on each node. The water-repellent, heart-shaped leaves hide the stem, which can sometimes produce white flowers with six petals. The more intense the light, the browner the leaves become.</p>"
    }
